===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[travel]] [[around]] along a curved path; to [[orbit]].
#: {{ux|en|The wolves '''circled''' the herd of deer.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Essay on Man|passage=Other planets '''circle''' other suns.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[surround]]; to encompass within a circle.
##: {{ux|en|A high fence '''circles''' the enclosure.}}
##: {{ux|en|The lightbulb '''circled''' the patio in light.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1699|author=w:William Dampier|title=Voyages and Descriptions
|passage=Their heads are '''circled''' with a short turban.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1798|author=w:Samuel Taylor Coleridge|title=[[s:Lyrical Ballads (1798)/The Dungeon|The Dungeon]]
|passage=So he lies, '''circled''' with evil.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To place in a circle; to make a circle.
#: {{ux|en|We '''circled''' stones around him.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[place]] or [[mark]] a circle around.
##: {{ux|en|'''Circle''' the jobs that you are interested in applying for.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To smoke [[cannabis]] in a circle, passing the cannabis around from person to person.
##: {{ux|en|We '''circled''' a joint that afternoon.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive|paganism}} To take part in a [[magic circle]].
##: {{ux|en|I '''circled''' with that group for three years.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To add someone to a circle on the social media site Google+.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To travel in circles.
#: {{syn|en|gyrate}} 
#: {{ux|en|Vultures '''circled''' overhead.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To move in a circle around a [[target]] in preparation for an [[attack]].
##: {{ux|en|The shark '''circled''' the diver for several minutes.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[circulate]].
##: {{ux|en|The rumor '''circled''' through the crowd.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} to [[consider]] or [[negotiate]] an agreement.
##: {{ux|en|A high-profile actor is '''circling''' the next Spielberg movie.}}
# {{lb|en|University of Warwick|_|slang}} To participate in a game of [[circling]].

