## A [[bedroom]].
## The [[private]] [[office]] of a [[judge]].
## The [[room]] used for [[deliberation]] by a [[legislature]].
## {{label|en|UK}} A single [[law]] [[office]] in a building housing several.
## {{label|en|dated|usually|in the plural}} Rooms in a [[lodging]] [[house]].
##* {{RQ:Thackeray Pendennis|II|Which Had Very Nearly Been the Last of the Story|120|A committee of marriageable ladies, or of any Christian persons interested in the propagation of the domestic virtues, should employ a Cruikshank or a Leech, or some other kindly expositor of the follies of the day, to make a series of designs representing the horrors of a bachelor's life in '''chambers''', and leading the beholder to think of better things, and a more wholesome condition.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} {{ellipsis of|en|chamber pot|t=a [[container]] used for [[urination]] and [[defecation]] in one's chambers}}.
