# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[place]] in a chamber, as a [[round]] of [[ammunition]].
#: {{ux|en|The hunter fired at the geese and missed, then shrugged his shoulders and '''chambered''' another cartridge.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[create]] or [[modify]] a [[gun]] to be a specific [[caliber]].
#: {{ux|en|The rifle was originally '''chambered''' for 9mm, but had since been modified for a larger, wildcat caliber.}}
# {{lb|en|martial arts|transitive}} To [[prepare]] an [[offensive]], [[defensive]], or [[counteroffensive]] action by drawing a [[limb]] or [[weapon]] to a position where it may be [[charged]] with [[kinetic energy]].
#: {{ux|en|Bob '''chambered''' his fist for a blow, but Sheila struck first.}}
