===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|physiology}} The [[part]]s of an [[animal]] [[body]] [[comprise|comprising]] the [[heart]], [[blood vessel]]s ([[artery|arteries]], [[vein#Noun|veins]]{{,}} and [[capillary#Noun|capillaries]]){{,}} and [[blood#Noun|blood]], which [[circulate]] the blood around the body. {{defdate|from mid 19th c.}}
#: {{synonyms|en|q1=by some writers|cardiovascular system|q2=by some writers|vascular system|q3=loosely|circulation}}
# {{lb|en|technology}} The parts of a [[machine]] [[responsible#Adjective|responsible]] for the {{l|en|circulation}} of some [[fluid]].

====Usage notes====
Some writers treat {{m|en|cardiovascular system}} and {{m|en|vascular system}} as synonymous with ''circulatory system''. Others regard these terms as {{glossary|hyponym}}s.

